s contains at least one character with an odd frequency and one with an even frequency.

Starter code:

class Solution:
    def maxDifference(self, s: str) -> int:


=== MODEL ===
Count character frequencies, then take the max odd frequency minus the min even frequency. Note that 0 counts as even, but only characters present in the string matter here, so I'll restrict to characters with nonzero frequency.

