class Solution:
    def generateString(self, str1: str, str2: str) -> str:


=== MODEL ===
This is the "generate string" problem. The approach: positions forced by 'T' constraints must match str2 exactly; conflicts mean no answer. Unconstrained characters start as 'a'. For each 'F' index, the window must differ from str2; if all its positions are forced-by-T and already equal str2, it's impossible, otherwise we bump the last free position in the window to the next letter that avoids equality—but to keep it lexicographically smallest, we set free positions to 'a' and then for each violated 'F' window, we change its last free position (which is safe because it doesn't affect earlier windows' T constraints, and setting it to 'b' breaks the match).

Let me write it carefully.
TOOL submit_solution {"ticket_id": "Q-7113", "code": "class Solution:\n    def generateString(self, str1: str, str2: str) -> str:\n        n, m = len(str1), len(str2)\n        L = n + m - 1\n        word = [None] * L\n        fixed = [False] * L\n\n        # Apply T constraints\n        for i, c in enumerate(str1):\n            if c == 'T':\n                for j in range(m):\n                    pos = i + j\n                    if fixed[pos]:\n                        if word[pos] != str2[j]:\n                            return \"\"\n                    else:\n                        fixed[pos] = True\n                        word[pos] = str2[j]\n\n        # Fill free positions with 'a'\n        for k in range(L):\n            if not fixed[k]:\n                word[k] = 'a'\n\n        def matches(i):\n            return all(word[i + j] == str2[j] for j in range(m))\n\n        # Satisfy F constraints\n        for i, c in enumerate(str1):\n            if c == 'F' and matches(i):\n                # find the last free position in window to change\n                changed = False\n                for j in range(m - 1, -1, -1):\n                    pos = i + j\n                    if not fixed[pos]:\n                        # choose smallest letter different from current value\n                        # that keeps it != str2[j]; 'a' or 'b' suffices\n                        word[pos] = 'b' if word[pos] == 'a' else 'a'\n                        changed = True\n                        break\n                if not changed:\n                    return \"\"\n\n        # Final verification\n        for i, c in enumerate(str1):\n            ok = matches(i)\n            if c == 'T' and not ok:\n                return \"\"\n            if c == 'F' and ok:\n                return \"\"\n\n        return \"\".join(word)\n"}

