Starter code:

class Solution:
    def shortestMatchingSubstring(self, s: str, p: str) -> int:


=== MODEL ===
Approach: split p by '*' into three parts: prefix a, middle b, suffix c (any may be empty). A substring matches if it starts with a, ends with c, and contains b in the middle at a position at or after the end of a, with the b-occurrence ending no later than the start of c's occurrence.

For each occurrence position i of a, and each occurrence position j of b with j ≥ i + len(a), take the earliest occurrence of c starting at k ≥ j + len(b). The substring spans from i to k + len(c). I'll use sorted occurrence lists with bisect to find, for each candidate i, the first valid j and then the first valid k.

Using the first valid j for each i is optimal since it gives the earliest end for b, and the first valid k after it gives the earliest end for c. Taking the minimum over all i gives the answer.

I'll find occurrences with KMP-style search (Python's `str.find` in a loop could be quadratic, so I'll use the prefix-function approach).
TOOL submit_solution {"ticket_id": "Q-7649", "code": "import bisect\n\nclass Solution:\n    def shortestMatchingSubstring(self, s: str, p: str) -> int:\n        def occurrences(text, pat):\n            # returns sorted list of starting indices where pat occurs in text (KMP)\n            if pat == \"\":\n                return list(range(len(text) + 1))\n            m = len(pat)\n            pi = [0] * m\n            k = 0\n            for q in range(1, m):\n                while k > 0 and pat[k] != pat[q]:\n                    k = pi[k - 1]\n                if pat[k] == pat[q]:\n                    k += 1\n                pi[q] = k\n            res = []\n            k = 0\n            for i, ch in enumerate(text):\n                while k > 0 and pat[k] != ch:\n                    k = pi[k - 1]\n                if pat[k] == ch:\n                    k += 1\n                if k == m:\n                    res.append(i - m + 1)\n                    k = pi[k - 1]\n            return res\n\n        first = p.find('*')\n        second = p.find('*', first + 1)\n        a = p[:first]\n        b = p[first + 1:second]\n        c = p[second + 1:]\n        la, lb, lc = len(a), len(b), len(c)\n\n        A = occurrences(s, a)\n        B = occurrences(s, b)\n        C = occurrences(s, c)\n        if not A or not B or not C:\n            return -1\n\n        best = -1\n        for i in A:\n            # b must start at j >= i + la\n            idx = bisect.bisect_left(B, i + la)\n            if idx >= len(B):\n                continue\n            j = B[idx]\n            # c must start at k >= j + lb\n            idx2 = bisect.bisect_left(C, j + lb)\n            if idx2 >= len(C):\n                continue\n            k = C[idx2]\n            length = k + lc - i\n            if best == -1 or length < best:\n                best = length\n        return best\n"}

